 "inferred_links": {
  "I1": "Mixer value text is read by the generic loader: plain decimal -> nearest binary64 -> nearest binary32, Booleans true/false, codes decimal. Not re-traced for TimeableFloat, TimeableBool, TimeableEnum or RemoteableEnum; tempo (TimeableSongTempo) is a different class, so the transport-state-v1 check does not carry over by identity. Fixture numbers are chosen so single and double rounding agree.",
  "I2": "The value text of an enumerated value is its entry name (PanMode, CrossFadeState, CrossfadeCurve); the enum text routine is not traced.",
  "I3": "LiveSet/CrossfadeCurve is the set enum the set constructor initialises with the seven names and index 2 (corpus 0x102672448); member-to-element binding untraced; consistent with 375/376 shipped sets storing 2.",
  "I4": "The platform log10f is within one binary32 step of the correctly rounded result; the 0.00005 dB margin and the two-step tolerance in model() cover it.",
  "I5": "Split pans use the pan text converter: 0x10271c734 pseudocode passes singleton 0x101439ec4 for Pan and both splits; the confirmed branch is Pan's.",
  "I6": "The primary text slot (+0x28: unit and -inf) is the value text a user sees in at least one place; the second slot (+0x40) form is excluded; covered by the comparison obligation.",
  "I7": "arm64 equivalence of the extracted functions within each comparison (fma-scan.txt).",
  "I8": "The reference exp10f rounds the round-trip curve points to nearest (margin >= 0.16 step, model).",
  "I9": "Apple exp10f and cos within one binary32 step of glibc at the case inputs (comparators allow one step).",
  "I10": "The template set opens: it meets every traced structural condition of SPEC-LIVE-SET-STRUCTURE r1 and writes every W element as T11-MIN does; it holds no clip, sample or device, so A4 and A6 are not involved; A5 concerns refusals and A7 saving only."
 },
